COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[543,"§Al-Mujadila\ndeeds\nSit with a Muslim to speak about a subject that will increase your faith, and converse privatly with him about righteousness and piety.\nThink positively about the believers, for secret talks come from evil assumptions.\nMake space for your brethren in a study circle and a gathering so that Allah will make space for you.\nguid\nRemember the limitless knowledge of Allah, and that nothing is hidden from Him.\nWhenever you grieve, know that it is coming from satan, as he means to make your heart grieve.\nRelying upon Allah is one of the remedies for grief.\nrefl\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ مَا يَكُونُ مِن نَّجۡوَىٰ ثَلَٰثَةٍ إِلَّا هُوَ رَابِعُهُمۡ وَلَا خَمۡسَةٍ إِلَّا هُوَ سَادِسُهُمۡ وَلَآ أَدۡنَىٰ مِن ذَٰلِكَ وَلَآ أَكۡثَرَ إِلَّا هُوَ مَعَهُمۡ أَيۡنَ مَا كَانُواْۖ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُم بِمَا عَمِلُواْ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِكُلِّ شَيۡءٍ عَلِيمٌ ٧\nThis verse begins and ends with mentioning knowledge, so Ibn Abbas, Ad-Dhahhak, Sufyan Al-Thawri, and Ahmad bin Hanbal said: Allah is with them by means of His knowledge. Ibn Taimyah: 6/241.\nHow do you infer from this verse (He is with them) that Allah is with them by means of His knowledge?\nوَإِذَا جَآءُوكَ حَيَّوۡكَ بِمَا لَمۡ يُحَيِّكَ بِهِ ٱللَّهُ\nWhen they used to come to the Prophet (ﷺ), they would whisper the word \"Salam\" because it is an Islamic rite that entails the meaning of safety, and replace it with \"Good day\", which was the Arab's greetings during the times of ignorance because they did not like to give up their old habits. Ibn Ashur: 28/31.\nWhat do you think of the widely used greetings among youth today? What is the best of all greetings?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا قِيلَ لَكُمۡ تَفَسَّحُواْ فِي ٱلۡمَجَٰلِسِ فَٱفۡسَحُواْ يَفۡسَحِ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡۖ\nThe ordained spacing is that which is done without standing up, and that is why Allah's Messenger said: \"A man should not ask another man to get up from his place in order to take his seat, but you should make room for each other and spread out.\" Ibn Juzay: 2/422.\nExplain the Islamic etiquette enjoined by this verse.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا قِيلَ لَكُمۡ تَفَسَّحُواْ فِي ٱلۡمَجَٰلِسِ فَٱفۡسَحُواْ يَفۡسَحِ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡۖ\n(Allah will make space for you), in your graves. It is said: In your hearts. Moreover, it is said that Allah will make space for you in this life and the Hereafter. Al-Qurtubi: 20/318.\nWhat is meant by (Allah will make space for you)?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا قِيلَ لَكُمۡ تَفَسَّحُواْ فِي ٱلۡمَجَٰلِسِ فَٱفۡسَحُواْ يَفۡسَحِ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡۖ\nThe reward is of the same nature as the deed, whoever makes space, Allah will make space for him, and whoever makes room for his brethren, Allah will make room for him. Al-Saadi: 846.\nGiven this verse, discuss this saying: The requital befits the action.\nيَرۡفَعِ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مِنكُمۡ وَٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ دَرَجَٰتٖۚ\nMeaning: Do not think that if one of you makes room for his brother, or rises up when he is commanded to do so, this will diminish his right or honor. Rather, this will increase his virtue and status with Allah. Ibn Kathir: 4/326.\nDoes making space for your brethren diminish your right?\nيَرۡفَعِ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مِنكُمۡ وَٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ دَرَجَٰتٖۚ\nMeaning: It is the knowledge with which Allah sent His Prophet (ﷺ), and if the scholars are given the same knowledge, then following them is obligatory. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/143.\nHow does this verse indicate the importance of following the scholars?\nwords\nبِمَا لَم يُحَيِّكَ بِهِ اللهُJews would greet you with \"Death be upon you,\" rather than \"Peace.\"\nلَولاَWhy does not\nحَسبُهُمSufficient for them\nالمَصِيرُDestination\nإِنَّمَا النَّجوَىSecret talks about sin and aggression\nتَفَسَّحُواMake space for one another\nانشُزُواArise from your gatherings"],[544,"§Al-Mujadila\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah for yor teacher or mentor who is patient in teaching you.\nAlways mention Allah's name before and after eating and sleeping.\nMaintain the five daily prayers in congregation, especially Al-Fajr and Al-Asr prayers.\nguid\nBe keen to follow the Prophet's (ﷺ) Sunnah.\nThe hypocrites are among the party of satan, so beware of them and their traits.\nLying, hypocrisy, and hatred for the Prophet’s (ﷺ) Companions are among the traits of the party of satan.\nrefl\nفَإِذۡ لَمۡ تَفۡعَلُواْ وَتَابَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ فَأَقِيمُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ\nAllah says, (establish prayer), and did not say, \"pray\" so that the aim is to fulfill all of the prayer's conditions, and complete it properly, not just to perform it. Al-Alusi: 14/225.\nAllah says, (establish prayer), and did not say, \"pray\". Why?\nفَأَقِيمُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتُواْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ\nEstablishing prayer and giving zakah are the most important physical and financial acts of worship. Whoever does them in the manner prescribed, has fulfilled his duty toward Allah and His servants. Al-Saadi: 847.\nAmong all acts of worship, establishing prayer and giving zakah are singled out for mention. Why?\nوَأَطِيعُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥۚ وَٱللَّهُ خَبِيرُۢ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ ١٣\n(And obey Allah and His Messenger), what matters in all of that is sincerity and doing them properly. Hence Allah says: (And Allah is All-Aware of what you do). Allah knows their deeds, how they were done and the intention behind them, so He will requite them according to his knowledge of what was in their hearts. Al-Saadi: 847.\nAfter enjoining us to obey Him, Allah describes Himself as All-Aware of what we do. Why?\n۞أَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ تَوَلَّوۡاْ قَوۡمًا غَضِبَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِم مَّا هُم مِّنكُمۡ وَلَا مِنۡهُمۡ\nAl-Qushayri said: Whoever joins those who incurred someone's wrath, falls under the wrath of that person, and whoever joins those who incurred Allah’s wrath, will fall under Allah's wrath, which is sufficient humiliation, sorrow and deprivation. Al-Biqai: 19/387.\nWhat is the risk of joining those who incurred Allah's wrath?\nيَوۡمَ يَبۡعَثُهُمُ ٱللَّهُ جَمِيعٗا فَيَحۡلِفُونَ لَهُۥ كَمَا يَحۡلِفُونَ لَكُمۡ وَيَحۡسَبُونَ أَنَّهُمۡ عَلَىٰ شَيۡءٍۚ أَلَآ إِنَّهُمۡ هُمُ ٱلۡكَٰذِبُونَ ١٨\nWhoever lives his life adhering to something, will die in that state. Just as the hypocrites tried to deceive the believers in this world, swearing to them that they were believers, on the Day of Resurrection, when Allah raises them all, they will swear to Allah as they swore to the believers, thinking that their oath would benefit them, because their disbelief, hypocrisy, and false beliefs kept sinking deeper and deeper into their minds until they were thoroughly deceived by them and thought that they were following something worthwhile that would bring them rewards. Al-Saadi: 848.\nThe hypocrites' ways in this life and the Hereafter are similar. How?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُحَآدُّونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥٓ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ فِي ٱلۡأَذَلِّينَ ٢٠\nThey oppose Allah and His Messenger because of their abundant followers, which makes those who are behind them believe that they possess the might that no one else has. Allah negates this apparent delusion by saying, (they), the lowlife and despicable (are among the most debased), they know that they are the most humiliated among people. Alhasan said: The sins have caused humiliation in their hearts despite their apparent vanities. Al-Biqai: 19/39.\nIn light of this verse, what is the effect of sins on the hearts?\nكَتَبَ ٱللَّهُ لَأَغۡلِبَنَّ أَنَا۠ وَرُسُلِيٓۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ قَوِيٌّ عَزِيزٞ ٢١\nAl-Zajjaj said: The prevalence of the Messengers was two types: Whoever was sent with force, prevails in war, and whoever was not sent with force, prevails by argument. Al-Baghawi: 4/349.\nHow did Allah's Messengers prevail over the deniers while some of the Messengers were killed by their people?\nwords\nالَّذِينَ تَوَلَّوا قَومًاHypocrites who take Jews as allies\nجُنَّةًShield against being killed\nوَيَحسَبُونَThey think\nاستَحوَذَTook hold, overcome\nيُحَآدُّونَOppose\nالأَذَلِّينَThe most debased\nلَأَغلِبَنَّI will surely prevail"],[545,"§Al-Mujadila, Al-Hashr\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask You for Your pleasure and Paradise.\"\nAsk Allah for guidance for your parents, brothers and kindred.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the distress of trial, being overtaken by a tribulation, gloating of enemies, and perversity of fate.\"\nguid\nEnsure that your brotherhood and love are for the sake of Allah, not for worldly gains.\nIt is important to oppose those who oppose Allah and His Messenger, even if they are close relatives.\nRegardless of their power, none can overcome the decree of Allah, the Almighty.\nrefl\nلَّا تَجِدُ قَوۡمٗا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ يُوَآدُّونَ مَنۡ حَآدَّ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ\nMeaning: Faith and close ties with the disbelievers cannot coexist. A person cannot truly be a believer in Allah and the Last Day unless he acts in accordance with what faith dictates and requires, of loving and taking as allies those who have faith, and resenting and opposing those who do not have faith. Al-Saadi: 848.\nFaith in Allah and the Last Day are linked to opposition to those who oppose Allah and His Messenger. How?\nلَّا تَجِدُ قَوۡمٗا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ يُوَآدُّونَ مَنۡ حَآدَّ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ\nAllah states that no true believer takes those who oppose Allah and His Messenger as allies because the essence of faith contradicts this alliance just as opposites repel one other. So if faith exists in the heart, then its opposite is negated, which is taking the enemies of Allah as allies. When one takes the enemies of Allah as allies, it proves that his heart does not possess the required faith. Ibn Taimyah: 6/257.\nAllah describes them as believers when He negated their alliance with those who oppose Allah and His Messenger. Why?\nرَضِيَ ٱللَّهُ عَنۡهُمۡ وَرَضُواْ عَنۡهُ\n(Allah is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him), this contains a beautiful secret, which is when the believers became enraged against their relatives and kindred in Allah's cause, He compensated them by being pleased with them and making them pleased with Him by granting them eternal delight and encompassing favor. Ibn Kathir: 4/32.\nIn light of this verse, explain the reason for Allah's pleasure with the believers and their pleasure with Him.\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ حِزۡبُ ٱللَّهِۚ أَلَآ إِنَّ حِزۡبَ ٱللَّهِ هُمُ ٱلۡمُفۡلِحُونَ ٢٢\n(They are), those who are at a higher level of greatness because they confine their alliance to Allah, as they know that good and harm are controlled only by Him. Al-Biqai: 19/400.\nWhat is the real sign of the party of Allah?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَخۡرَجَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ مِن دِيَٰرِهِمۡ لِأَوَّلِ ٱلۡحَشۡرِۚ\nDo not rely on other than Allah like these hypocrites did. Whoever relies on a created being, will be let down and end up in humiliation. Al-Biqai: 19/411.\nWhat is the consequence of relying on a created being instead of Allah?\nوَظَنُّوٓاْ أَنَّهُم مَّانِعَتُهُمۡ حُصُونُهُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ فَأَتَىٰهُمُ ٱللَّهُ مِنۡ حَيۡثُ لَمۡ يَحۡتَسِبُواْۖ\nThey were proud and deluded by them, and they thought that they would not be harmed and that no one could breach them, and they were content with them, but whoever puts his trust in anything other than Allah will be let down, and whoever turns to anyone but Allah, will be doomed. Al-Saadi: 849.\nThis verse exhorts people to rely on Allah, not on the means. Explain\nيُخۡرِبُونَ بُيُوتَهُم بِأَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَأَيۡدِي ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ فَٱعۡتَبِرُواْ يَٰٓأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرِ ٢\nMeaning: Contemplate the end of those who defied Allah's command, opposed His Messenger, and denied His Book. See how Allah's humiliating torment struck them in this life, as well as, the painful torment that Allah has reserved for them in the Hereafter. Ibn Kathir: 4/331.\nWhat is the lesson learned from the story of Bani Al-Nadheer?\nwords\nيُوَآدُّونَHaving affection for\nحَآدَّOpposes\nعَشِيرَتَهُمTheir relatives\nوَأَيَّدَهُمHe strengthened them\nبِرُوحٍ مِنهُWith help and victory\nلَم يَحتَسِبُواThey had not expected\nوَقَذَفَHe cast"],[546,"§Al-Hashr\ndeeds\nGive a gift to a new Muslim or a foreign student.\nShare your breakfast today with a needy person, in pursuit of Allah's reward.\nSay, \"O Allah, protect me from the covetousness of my soul.\"\nguid\nAdhere to what the Prophet's (ﷺ) Sunnah enjoins and forbids.\nTruthfulness may require some sacrifice.\nA successful person is the one who is protected from the covetousness of his soul.\nrefl\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ شَآقُّواْ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥۖ وَمَن يُشَآقِّ ٱللَّهَ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ ٤\n(And whoever opposes Allah, Allah is truly severe in punishment): Here, He limits the opposition to Allah only because opposing Him is an opposition to His Messenger. Al-Shawkani: 5/196.\nThis verse limits the opposition to Allah only. Why?\nكَيۡ لَا يَكُونَ دُولَةَۢ بَيۡنَ ٱلۡأَغۡنِيَآءِ مِنكُمۡۚ\nSo that the wealth bestowed by Allah does not become a perpetual distribution among the rich and powerful leaders, while the weak and poor are left out. During the times of ignorance [pre-Islam], the head of the tribe used to take one-fourth of the spoils of war for himself, hence, Allah allocated this to His Messenger to divide it as He commands. Al-Baghawi: 4/357.\nWhat is meant by (So that wealth should not circulate only among those of you who are rich)?\nوَمَآ ءَاتَىٰكُمُ ٱلرَّسُولُ فَخُذُوهُ وَمَا نَهَىٰكُمۡ عَنۡهُ فَٱنتَهُواْۚ\nThis verse ends with the command to obey the Messenger (ﷺ) to remove what may reside in the souls of some in the Muslim army from being deprived of the booties bestowed by Allah upon His Messenger (ﷺ) from the land of Bani Al-Nadheer. Ibn Ashur: 28/86.\nThis verse ends with the command to obey the Messenger (ﷺ). Why?\nوَلَا يَجِدُونَ فِي صُدُورِهِمۡ حَاجَةٗ مِّمَّآ أُوتُواْ وَيُؤۡثِرُونَ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ وَلَوۡ كَانَ بِهِمۡ خَصَاصَةٞۚ\nAllah relates that they gave what they had for charity despite their need, and they did not resent what their brethren were given. Based on that, they were free of stinginess and envy, and that is why stinginess and envy are of the same type, because an envious person does not like the giving by some to others while a stingy person does not like giving out of his own wealth. Ibn Taimyah: 6/272.\nThis verse mentions two great traits of the believers. What are they?\nوَيُؤۡثِرُونَ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ وَلَوۡ كَانَ بِهِمۡ خَصَاصَةٞ\nThe preference of others over oneself applies to worldly gains, not to the times spent in doing righteous deeds, as being stingy with such times is a true success. Whoever does not preserve his time, people will leave him in ruin. Preserving one's time is protecting one's heart and his greatest asset is his life. This is indicated by Allah's command to race one another and compete against each other in doing righteous deeds, which is the opposite of preferring others to oneself. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/146.\nWhen is preferring others to oneself considered a good thing? When is stinginess considers good?\nوَيُؤۡثِرُونَ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ وَلَوۡ كَانَ بِهِمۡ خَصَاصَةٞ\nThis level of faith is higher than that of those whom Allah described in these verses, (And they give food, despite their love for it) [76:8], and, (And gives his wealth, in spite of love for it) [2:177]. These give charity despite their love for their wealth, however, they are not in need for it, nor it is necessary for them to keep. The former prefer others to themselves even though they are in need and have a necessity for what they spend in charity. Ibn Kathir: 4/338.\nWho is better: One who prefers others to himself, or one who gives charity despite his loves for it?\nوَمَن يُوقَ شُحَّ نَفۡسِهِۦ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُفۡلِحُونَ ٩\nIf a person is protected from his own covetousness, he will be at ease with the commands of Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ), and will comply with them obediently and willingly, with an open heart, and he will be at ease with refraining from what Allah forbids, even if it is dear to him and his heart longs for it. He will be at ease with spending his wealth in Allah's cause, seeking His pleasure. Thus, he will attain success and triumph. Al-Saadi: 851.\nProtection from the covetousness of one's soul is a reason for success. How?\nwords\nلِينَةٍA palm tree\nوَمَا أَفَاءَ اللهWealth bestowed by Allah upon you without war\nفَمَا أَوجَفتُمYou did not spur on any ride for that\nرِكَابٍCamels\nدُولَةًCirculating ownership\nتَبَوَّءُوا الدَّارَThose who were settled in Madinah"],[547,"§Al-Hashr\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah by saying:\nSeek refuge with Allah from the accursed satan and his whisperings.\nDraw three traits of the hypocrites from theses verses.\nguid\nIt is important to clear one's heart from ill feeling toward the people of faith.\nFright and cowardice are permanent characteristics of Jews.\nFearing people more than Allah is a sign of ignorance.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ جَآءُو مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا ٱغۡفِرۡ لَنَا وَلِإِخۡوَٰنِنَا ٱلَّذِينَ سَبَقُونَا بِٱلۡإِيمَٰنِ وَلَا تَجۡعَلۡ فِي قُلُوبِنَا غِلّٗا لِّلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ رَبَّنَآ إِنَّكَ رَءُوفٞ رَّحِيمٌ ١٠\nIt is said that these are the Companions' followers and their followers who came afterward until the Day of Resurrection. Based on that, Imam Malik said: Whoever reviles the Companions, will have no share in the booties with or without war, because Allah describes those who come after the Companions as: (They say, \"Our Lord, forgive us and our brethren who preceded us in faith\"), hence, whoever says the opposite of that, will be out of those described by Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/430.\nHow did Imam Malik deduce from this verse that whoever reviles the Companions, has no share in the booties?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ جَآءُو مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا ٱغۡفِرۡ لَنَا وَلِإِخۡوَٰنِنَا ٱلَّذِينَ سَبَقُونَا بِٱلۡإِيمَٰنِ\nThis is one of the virtues of faith, that the believers seek to benefit from one another and pray for one another because of their shared faith which creates the bond of brotherhood between the believers. One of the branches of that brotherhood is that they pray for one another and love one another. Al-Saadi: 852.\nThis verse indicates one of the virtues of faith. What is it?\nلَأَنتُمۡ أَشَدُّ رَهۡبَةٗ فِي صُدُورِهِم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَوۡمٞ لَّا يَفۡقَهُونَ ١٣\nThe true understanding is to fear the Creator, put one's hope in Him and love Him, and give precedence to this over all other matters, which should be secondary to it. Al-Saadi: 852.\nWhat is the sign of the servant's understanding?\nلَأَنتُمۡ أَشَدُّ رَهۡبَةٗ فِي صُدُورِهِم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِۚ\nThe fear is described as: In their hearts, which indicates that it was very hidden. Meaning: They pretended to ready themselves for fighting the Muslims, and bluffed their courage to frighten them, but, in fact, they were not up to it, and Allah disclosed their true nature to His Messenger (ﷺ). Ibn Ashur: 28/103.\nThe fear is described as: In their hearts, why? How does it benefit the Muslims?\nبَأۡسُهُم بَيۡنَهُمۡ شَدِيدٞۚ تَحۡسَبُهُمۡ جَمِيعٗا وَقُلُوبُهُمۡ شَتَّىٰۚ\nAl-Qushayri said: Meeting people with discordant hearts is the basis of degeneration, forsaking, and enticing the enemy to be more daring against them. In contrast, harmony of the hearts, unified resolve, and common purpose bring about success and happiness. Al-Biqai: 19/452.\nWhat is the risk of discordant hearts?\nبَأۡسُهُم بَيۡنَهُمۡ شَدِيدٞۚ تَحۡسَبُهُمۡ جَمِيعٗا وَقُلُوبُهُمۡ شَتَّىٰۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَوۡمٞ لَّا يَعۡقِلُونَ ١٤\nThey are lacking faith that keeps them together, for they know that they follow falsehood and desires, which keep them divided. Unlike reason, which is the basis for unity, following whims is the basis for division. Al-Biqai: 19/453.\nThe Jews are described as: A people who do not reason. Why?\nبَأۡسُهُم بَيۡنَهُمۡ شَدِيدٞۚ تَحۡسَبُهُمۡ جَمِيعٗا وَقُلُوبُهُمۡ شَتَّىٰۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَوۡمٞ لَّا يَعۡقِلُونَ ١٤\nThis verse contains a lesson to Muslims to beware of disputes and hostilities among themselves, and to realize that the strength of the Muslim Ummah against its enemies stems from its unity. Ibn Ashur: 28/106.\nThe verse indicates the importance of unity against enemies. Explain.\nwords\nغِلًاEnvy, ill feeling\nلإِخوَانِهِمُThe Jews of Bani Al-Nadheer\nجُدُرٍWalls\nبَأسُهُم بَينَهُمThe enmity among themselves\nشَتَّىDiverse\nوَبَالَ أَمرِهِمThe evil consequence of their disbelief\nكَمَثَلِ الشَّيطَانِThe hypocrites are like the example of satan"],[548,"§Al-Hashr\ndeeds\nReflect on your actions of last week, think of three good deeds that you had completed, and show your gratitude and thanks to Allah for them. Then think of three mistakes and ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nEnsure, today, that you read the supplications of entering and exiting your house, and the daily remembrance (Athkar) in the morning and evening.\nSupplicate Allah by His Holy Names that are cited in this Surah.\nguid\nAlways remember the Day of Resurrection and keep it present in your mind.\nCauses of piety are many of which is remembering the Last Day and sensing the greatness of Allah.\nEnsure that you maintain humbleness when reciting the Holy Quran.\nrefl\nوَلۡتَنظُرۡ نَفۡسٞ مَّا قَدَّمَتۡ لِغَدٖۖ\n(Sent) is a verb in the past tense form to urge one to do good deeds for the Hereafter and not delay, for he has nothing except what he had done in the past. He can't control the future and does not know what will transpire. (No soul knows what it will do tomorrow) [31:34]. Al-Shanqiti: 8/54.\nThe verb “sent” is in past tense. Why?\nوَلۡتَنظُرۡ نَفۡسٞ مَّا قَدَّمَتۡ لِغَدٖۖ\nThis verse offers a guideline with regard to doing self-reckoning and reminds the believer that he should continue to check on himself and if he sees any lapse, he must take action by giving it up, repenting sincerely and turning away from any means that may lead to it. If he sees himself falling short with regard to any divine command, he should strive hard and seek the help of his Lord in completing, perfecting, and doing it properly. He should compare the blessings that Allah has bestowed generously upon him with his shortcomings, for that will undoubtedly make him feel humbled. Al-Saadi: 853.\nExplain self-reckoning in light of this verse.\nوَلَا تَكُونُواْ كَٱلَّذِينَ نَسُواْ ٱللَّهَ فَأَنسَىٰهُمۡ أَنفُسَهُمۡۚ\nWhen Allah makes one forget himself, it means making him forget his own self high gains, the means to one's satisfaction, prosperity, reform and everything that leads to one's excellence. He makes him forget all of that to a point where they never cross his mind or become desirable to him. Moreover, Allah makes him forget his own flaws and shortcomings so that he becomes heedless of eliminating them. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/147.\nHow does one forget himself?\nوَلَا تَكُونُواْ كَٱلَّذِينَ نَسُواْ ٱللَّهَ فَأَنسَىٰهُمۡ أَنفُسَهُمۡۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡفَٰسِقُونَ ١٩\n(He made them forget themselves), as if the listener asked: What was the result of making them forget themselves? My answer is: Because of it, they have reached the farthest level of defiant disobedience with their evil deeds where one can say that nothing else can match their defiant disobedience. Ibn Ashur: 28/114.\nWhat was the result of making them forget themselves?\nلَوۡ أَنزَلۡنَا هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ عَلَىٰ جَبَلٖ لَّرَأَيۡتَهُۥ خَٰشِعٗا مُّتَصَدِّعٗا مِّنۡ خَشۡيَةِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nAllah urges Mankind to reflect on the admonitions of the Quran and makes clear that it is inexcusable to omit reflecting on it. If the mountains were mindful and were spoken to with this Quran, they would have followed its admonitions, and you would have seen these solid mountains humbled and splitting (cracking) in awe of Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 20/388.\nIs there an excuse for anyone to omit reflecting on the Quran after reciting this verse?\nهُوَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِي لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَۖ عَٰلِمُ ٱلۡغَيۡبِ وَٱلشَّهَٰدَةِۖ هُوَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٢٢\nSince this attribute (Knower of the unseen and the seen) is unique to Allah that no one else shares with Him, it is stated as evidence of the Oneness of Allah in other verses of the Quran. Al-Shanqiti: 8/68.\nWhat is the evidence of the Oneness of Allah?\nهُوَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِي لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ٱلۡمَلِكُ ٱلۡقُدُّوسُ ٱلسَّلَٰمُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُ\nAllah, the Almighty, is the Sovereign (the King) but is unlike other kings who are known to be flawed as one may think. So, His name (the Most Holy) is exalting Him above all flaws and imperfections, His name (the Believer/Grantor of security) is exalting His unseen actions above treachery and deception, and His name (the Most Perfect/Source of peace) is exalting His visible actions above tyranny and injustice. Ibn Ashur: 28/121.\nThe Holy Names: (the Most Holy), (the Most Perfect) and (the Believer) are stated after Allah's name (the Sovereign). Why?\nwords\nوَلتَنظُرLet every soul reflect\nفَأَنسَاهُم أَنفُسَهُمHe made them forget themselves\nمُتَصَدِّعًاSplitting\nوَالشَّهَادَةِAnd the seen\nالمُؤمِنُThe Believer who makes His Messengers believable with miracles and clear signs"],[549,"§Al-Mumtahanah\ndeeds\nSay, \"Our Lord, let our spouses and children be a source of joy for us, and make us good examples for the righteous.\"\nSay: [Our Lord, upon You we have relied, and to You we have returned, and to You is the final return]\nSupplicate Allah by saying: [Our Lord, do not make us subject to the persecution of those who disbelieve; and forgive us, our Lord. Indeed, You are the All-Mighty, the All-Wise]\nguid\nBeware of the disbelievers' plans and plots to weaken the Muslims' allegiance to Islam.\nNeither your relatives nor your children will benefit you if you neglect Allah's commands for them.\nRely on Allah and entrust your affairs to Him.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَتَّخِذُواْ عَدُوِّي وَعَدُوَّكُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءَ تُلۡقُونَ إِلَيۡهِم بِٱلۡمَوَدَّةِ\nFor once affection is formed, it will be followed by support and taking the friend as an ally. This puts a person beyond the pale of faith, and he will become one of the disbelievers; he will no longer be part of the community of faith. Al-Saadi: 855.\nHaving affection toward the disbelievers is prohibited. Why?\nوَأَنَا۠ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَآ أَخۡفَيۡتُمۡ وَمَآ أَعۡلَنتُمۡ\nMeaning: There is no point in concealment if you know that I Am All-Aware of it, but if you assume that I do not know it, then you are doomed. Al-Biqai: 19/488.\nWhat is the benefit of being aware that Allah knows what is concealed and what is declared. Why?\nإِن يَثۡقَفُوكُمۡ يَكُونُواْ لَكُمۡ أَعۡدَآءٗ وَيَبۡسُطُوٓاْ إِلَيۡكُمۡ أَيۡدِيَهُمۡ وَأَلۡسِنَتَهُم بِٱلسُّوٓءِ وَوَدُّواْ لَوۡ تَكۡفُرُونَ ٢\nThe faith of the believers is more valuable to them than their souls because they sacrifice them for it, and the enemy's highest priority is targeting the most valuable thing that his opponent has. Al-Alusi: 14/263.\nWhat is the most valuable thing to the believers? What is the enemy’s most priority?\nلَن تَنفَعَكُمۡ أَرۡحَامُكُمۡ وَلَآ أَوۡلَٰدُكُمۡۚ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ يَفۡصِلُ بَيۡنَكُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ بَصِيرٞ ٣\nWhen Hatib apologized by saying that he had children and relatives in Makkah, Allah made clear that family and children will not avail a person anything on the Day of Resurrection if he disobeyed Allah for them. Al-Qurtubi: 20/402.\nCan a Muslim be excused for spying against Muslims for fear for himself, children, or wealth?\nقَدۡ كَانَتۡ لَكُمۡ أُسۡوَةٌ حَسَنَةٞ فِيٓ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ وَٱلَّذِينَ مَعَهُۥٓ إِذۡ قَالُواْ لِقَوۡمِهِمۡ إِنَّا بُرَءَٰٓؤُاْ مِنكُمۡ وَمِمَّا تَعۡبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ كَفَرۡنَا بِكُمۡ وَبَدَا بَيۡنَنَا وَبَيۡنَكُمُ ٱلۡعَدَٰوَةُ وَٱلۡبَغۡضَآءُ أَبَدًا حَتَّىٰ تُؤۡمِنُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَحۡدَهُ\nLove for the sake of Allah and dislike for the sake of Allah are the strongest bonds of faith, hence, Muslims should not be heedless of them. Al-Alusi: 14/263.\nWhat are the strongest bonds of faith?\nقَدۡ كَانَتۡ لَكُمۡ أُسۡوَةٌ حَسَنَةٞ فِيٓ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ وَٱلَّذِينَ مَعَهُ\nMeaning: Muslims should follow their Messenger (ﷺ) just like those with Abraham (u) did with him. Ibn Ashur: 28/143.\nAllah enjoins the believers to follow the example of Abraham (u) and those with him. Why?\nرَبَّنَا لَا تَجۡعَلۡنَا فِتۡنَةٗ لِّلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ\nMeaning: Do not give them power over us because of our sins, so that they persecute and prevent us as much as they can from exercising our faith, which would cause them further confusion, for if they see that they have the upper hand, they would think that they are following the right path and that we are following the wrong path, and they will increase their disbelief and tyranny. Al-Saadi: 856.\nHow does the Muslim become a trial for the disbeliever?\nwords\nأَولِيَاءَClose associates, friends\nتُلقُونَExtending to them\nيَثقَفُوكُمThey gain dominance over you\nوَيَبسُطُواThey extend\nيَفصِلُ بَينَكُمHe will judge between you\nأُسوَةٌAn example\nأَنَبنَاWe returned in repentance\nالمَصِيرُFinal return"],[550,"§Al-Mumtahanah\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to guide the misguided and disbelievers.\nGive a gift to a disbeliever so that his heart may be attracted to Islam.\nRecall a Muslim whom you wronged, then apologize to him, or pray to Allah for him.\nguid\nA role model is very important in the Muslim's life.\nIt is permitted to treat with kindness a disbeliever who is non-combative.\nFairness and justice must be carried out with allies and opponents.\nrefl\nوَمَن يَتَوَلَّ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ هُوَ ٱلۡغَنِيُّ ٱلۡحَمِيدُ ٦\n(And whoever turns away) from Islam and acceptance of these admonishments, (then indeed, Allah is the Free of need), for He does not need their worship. (The Praiseworthy) in Himself and His attributes. Al-Qurtubi: 20/405.\nThe verse concludes with two holy names of Allah. Why?\n۞عَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَجۡعَلَ بَيۡنَكُمۡ وَبَيۡنَ ٱلَّذِينَ عَادَيۡتُم مِّنۡهُم\nDespite the kinship ties between them and the disbelievers, Muslims adhered to Allah's command to resent and boycott the disbelievers, and Allah knew their sincerity so He wanted to please them with this verse, where He promised that He will bring about affection between them. This was fulfilled, and the affection was completed after the conquest of Makkah when most of the Quraish tribe members accepted Islam. Ibn Juzay: 2/436.\nWhat is the link between this verse and disassociation from the disbelievers?\n۞عَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَجۡعَلَ بَيۡنَكُمۡ وَبَيۡنَ ٱلَّذِينَ عَادَيۡتُم مِّنۡهُم مَّوَدَّةٗۚ وَٱللَّهُ قَدِيرٞۚ\n(Perhaps Allah will bring about affection between you and those of them whom you hold as enemies), the cause of which will be their turning to faith. (Allah is Most Capable), which includes His being able to guide people's hearts and change them from one state to another. Al-Saadi: 856.\n(Allah is Most Capable) is mentioned after stating the possibility of changing the polytheists' enmity to affection. Why?\nلَّا يَنۡهَىٰكُمُ ٱللَّهُ عَنِ ٱلَّذِينَ لَمۡ يُقَٰتِلُوكُمۡ فِي ٱلدِّينِ وَلَمۡ يُخۡرِجُوكُم مِّن دِيَٰرِكُمۡ أَن تَبَرُّوهُمۡ وَتُقۡسِطُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُقۡسِطِينَ ٨\nAfter Allah mentions what the believers should do concerning the resentment toward the disbelievers and neglecting their friendship, He details who, among the disbelievers, should be treated with kindness and who should not, so He says, (Allah does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion). Al-Shawkani: 5/213.\nWhat is the link between this verse and the one before?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا جَآءَكُمُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتُ مُهَٰجِرَٰتٖ فَٱمۡتَحِنُوهُنَّۖ\nAl-Qushayri said: In general, probing is a way to awareness and the gems inside a soul become manifest by a trial, and whoever ventures upon something without experience, regrets it. Al-Biqai: 19/514.\nProbing the inside of the souls is important. Why?\nفَإِنۡ عَلِمۡتُمُوهُنَّ مُؤۡمِنَٰتٖ فَلَا تَرۡجِعُوهُنَّ إِلَى ٱلۡكُفَّارِۖ\nThis verse indicates that faith can be recognized and affirmed. Ibn Kathir: 4/351\nIs it possible to affirm the faith of some people?\nفَإِنۡ عَلِمۡتُمُوهُنَّ مُؤۡمِنَٰتٖ فَلَا تَرۡجِعُوهُنَّ إِلَى ٱلۡكُفَّارِۖ لَا هُنَّ حِلّٞ لَّهُمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحِلُّونَ لَهُنَّۖ وَءَاتُوهُم مَّآ أَنفَقُواْۚ\nAllah enjoins that if a Muslim woman [who is married to a disbeliever] is retained [by Muslims], her husband should be compensated for his expenditures [dowry]. This is considered a fulfilment of the covenant, since he is deprived of his wife due to an Islamic prohibition, it is obligatory to return his money to lessen his loss. Al-Qurtubi: 20/414\nState an example of a fulfilment of the covenant from this verse.\nwords\nيَرجُو اللهَHe hopes for Allah's reward\nيَتَوَلَّTurns away from following the Prophets\nالحَمِيدُThe Praiseworthy\nوَتُقسِطُواActing justly toward them\nوَظَاهَرُواThey helped\nأَن تَوَلَّوهُمTaking them as allies\nفَامتَحِنُوهُنّExamine their sincerity in faith"],[551,"§As-Saff, Al-Mumtahanah\ndeeds\nGlorify Allah a hundred times.\nChoose a righteous deed and act upon it, then share a message with your friends in which you encourage them to do the same, so that you will be among those who practice what they say.\nThink of a scholar or a preacher who was subjected to abuse and mention his virtues to your friends.\nguid\nOrganize your life, for Allah loves those who fight in His cause in rows, and He loves those who line up well for prayer.\nThe Prophets endured harm patiently, and they are role models for the preachers.\nBeware of deviating from the obedience to Allah, the Almighty, for it is a cause for a deviation of the heart.\nrefl\nوَلَا يَعۡصِينَكَ فِي مَعۡرُوفٖ\nDisobeying the Messenger (ﷺ) can only be in what is right because he never enjoins evil, but it is said that this is a proof that obeying those in authority is obligatory only in what is right. Ibn Taimyah: 6/295.\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) never enjoins evil, so why the verse limits the prohibition of disobeying him to what is right?\nوَلَا يَعۡصِينَكَ فِي مَعۡرُوفٖ\nMeaning: They will not disobey you in any right that you enjoin upon them, and in any wrong that you forbid them. Limiting the prohibition of disobeying him to what is right, even though the Messenger (ﷺ) does not enjoin except what is right, is to alert to the fundamental principle: There is no obedience to any created being if it involves disobedience to the Creator. Al-Alusi: 14/274.\nLimiting the prohibition of disobeying him to what is right, even though the Messenger (ﷺ) does not enjoin except what is right. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لِمَ تَقُولُونَ مَا لَا تَفۡعَلُونَ ٢\nAl-Nakhai said: Three verses in the Quran prevented me from narrating to people: (Do you enjoin righteousness upon people while you forget yourselves) [2:44], (And I do not want to go against what I am forbidding you) [11:88], and (O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do). Al-Qurtubi: 20/436.\nThe righteous predecessors feared this verse immensely. Explain.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لِمَ تَقُولُونَ مَا لَا تَفۡعَلُونَ ٢\nThe one who enjoins good should be the first one to hasten to do it, and the one who forbids evil should be the furthest removed of all people from it. Al-Saadi: 858.\nWhat is the lesson learned by the believing preacher from this verse?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحِبُّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُقَٰتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِهِۦ صَفّٗا كَأَنَّهُم بُنۡيَٰنٞ مَّرۡصُوصٞ ٤\nTheir rows should be organized in an orderly fashion, so that they stand side-by-side and shoulder to shoulder, striking dread into the hearts of the enemy, and offering encouragement to one another. Al-Saadi: 858.\nWhat is the wisdom behind standing in firm ranks as a solid structure for battle?\nكَأَنَّهُم بُنۡيَٰنٞ مَّرۡصُوصٞ ٤\nQatadah said: Do you not see how a builder does not like his building to be crooked? Similarly, Allah does not like His command to be changed. He lined up the believers on the battlefield and in their prayers, so adhere to His command, as it is a protection for those who do. Ibn Kathir: 4/359.\nAllah commands the believers to line up in an orderly fashion in two cases. What are they?\nفَلَمَّا زَاغُوٓاْ أَزَاغَ ٱللَّهُ قُلُوبَهُمۡ\nThis verse shows us that if Allah allows His servants to go astray, this is not injustice on His part, and they cannot use that as an argument against Him. Rather, it is their own fault, for they are the ones who closed the door of guidance to themselves after they came to know of it, hence, Allah requites them after that by causing them to go astray and deviate, which they have no way to ward off. Al-Saadi: 859.\nThis verse responds to those who claim that their misguidance is caused by fate. Explain.\nwords\nيُبَايِعنَكَPledging to you\nبِبُهتَانٍ يَفتَرِينَهُFalsely attributing illegitimate children to their husbands\nلاَ تَتَوَلَّواDo not take as allies\nكَبُرَ مَقتًاIt is most loathsome\nمَرصُوصٌA solid structure with no gaps\nزَاغُواThey deviated from the truth"],[552,"§As-Saff\ndeeds\nAmong the types of Jihad is striving with one's wealth for the sake of goodness and the welfare of the Muslim Ummah, so donate some of your money to a party you believe will work to raise the status of the Ummah.\nInvite a disbeliever to Islam.\nSupplicate Allah, the Almighty, to make you one of the supporters of His cause.\nguid\nBeware of fabricating lies against Allah, the Almighty.\nPursue the profitable trade that is mentioned in this verse.\nFollow the example of past nations in good deeds.\nrefl\nيُرِيدُونَ لِيُطۡفِـُٔواْ نُورَ ٱللَّهِ بِأَفۡوَٰهِهِمۡ\nMeaning: The disbelievers will try to contradict the truth with falsehood. Their attempts are similar to one's attempt to extinguish the sun with his mouth, which is impossible. Likewise, is the case of their attempt to extinguish the truth. Ibn Kathir: 4/361.\nExplain the analogy presented in this verse.\nوَٱللَّهُ مُتِمُّ نُورِهِۦ وَلَوۡ كَرِهَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ ٨\nThis statement (Will complete His light) is joined with the statement (they want), which indicates that they will never achieve their aim and that this religion will be complete and will prevail. Ibn Ashur: 28/190.\nWhat are the glad tidings contained in this verse (But Allah will complete His light)?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَرۡسَلَ رَسُولَهُۥ بِٱلۡهُدَىٰ وَدِينِ ٱلۡحَقِّ لِيُظۡهِرَهُۥ عَلَى ٱلدِّينِ كُلِّهِۦ وَلَوۡ كَرِهَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكُونَ ٩\nIt is well known that Allah promised to make Islam prevail over all religions; a prevalence of its knowledge and clarification, and a prevalence by the sword and spike. Allah says, (It is He who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to make it prevail over all religions). The scholars interpreted its prevalence by both, since the prevalence of guidance is through Knowledge and the prevalence of religion is through physical strength. Ibn Taimyah: 6/297.\nHow will the religion of Islam prevail over all religions?\nتُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَتُجَٰهِدُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ بِأَمۡوَٰلِكُمۡ وَأَنفُسِكُمۡۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡ إِن كُنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ١١\nIt is as if the souls had become stingy with their lives and survival, hence, He says, (That is best for you, if you only knew), which means that Jihad is much better for you than remaining in this life and safety. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/153.\nThe verse concludes with (if you only knew). Why?\nتُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَتُجَٰهِدُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ بِأَمۡوَٰلِكُمۡ وَأَنفُسِكُمۡۚ\nIt is well known that perfect faith is to believe with certainty in what Allah has commanded us to believe in, which requires physical actions, one of the most sublime of which is Jihad in Allah's cause. Hence Allah says: (And strive in the cause of Allah with your wealth and your lives). Al-Saadi: 860.\nWhat is the link between faith and Jihad?\nيَغۡفِرۡ لَكُمۡ ذُنُوبَكُمۡ وَيُدۡخِلۡكُمۡ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ وَمَسَٰكِنَ طَيِّبَةٗ فِي جَنَّٰتِ عَدۡنٖۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡفَوۡزُ ٱلۡعَظِيمُ ١٢\nThe dwellings are mentioned here because they leave their homes behind when they go for Jihad, hence, Allah promised them eternal and pleasant homes for their brief departure from their own. Ibn Ashur: 28/195.\nThe dwellings are singled out for mention. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ كُونُوٓاْ أَنصَارَ ٱللَّهِ\nAllah, the Exalted, orders His faithful servants to be supporters of His cause in all situations, through their words, actions, selves, and wealth. Ibn Kathir: 4/361.\nIs the support for Allah's cause limited to a particular time or situation?\nwords\nافتَرَىFabricates\nنُورَ اللهِwas sent (ﷺ) The Truth with which Allah's Messenger\nبِأَفوَاهِهِمWith their lies\nمُتِمُّ نُورِهِHe makes the Truth [His religion] prevail\nالدِّينِ كُلِّهِAll other opposing religions\nلِلحَوَارِيِّينَThe disciples of Jesus (u)\nظَاهِرِينَThey prevailed"],[553,"§Al-Jumu'ah\ndeeds\nCall upon Allah by His names, the Most Holy, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise, and learn their impact on your faith.\nDo an act of goodness discretely.\nAsk Allah for a good end to your life.\nguid\nThe preacher's mission is to educate people in the knowledge and practice of the Quran and Sunnah.\nPursue and maintain self-purification.\nThe example of those who do not practice what they know is terrible.\nrefl\nيُسَبِّحُ لِلَّهِ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ ٱلۡمَلِكِ ٱلۡقُدُّوسِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ١\nIn this Surah, the verb (glorifies) is in the present tense, while in other Surahs it is in the past tense, to allude to the importance of Al-Jumu'ah prayer and denounce those who interrupted their prayer and went for some merchandise or amusement. Hence, it is pertinent to assert all that is in the heavens and earth glorifies Allah constantly and without interruption, unlike those who did not complete Al-Jumu'ah prayer. Ibn Ashur: 28/206.\nIn this Surah, the verb (glorifies) is in the present tense, while in other Surahs it is in the past tense. Why?\nيُسَبِّحُ لِلَّهِ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ\nAllah states that everything in the heavens and the earth glorifies His praises, including all types of living creatures and inanimate objects. Ibn Kathir: 4/363.\nDo only speaking creatures glorify Allah?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي بَعَثَ فِي ٱلۡأُمِّيِّۧنَ رَسُولٗا مِّنۡهُمۡ يَتۡلُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ وَيُزَكِّيهِمۡ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ وَإِن كَانُواْ مِن قَبۡلُ لَفِي ضَلَٰلٖ مُّبِينٖ ٢\nReciting is mentioned first because conveying the revelation begins with reciting. Purification comes second since calling others to Allah entails purifying their souls from the impurity of polytheism and relevant evil words, actions, and habits. Teaching comes next because it is after receiving the Book, that its aims and meanings are explained and clarified. Ibn Ashur: 28/209.\nThe statement begins with reciting, purifying, then, teaching the Book and Wisdom. Why?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي بَعَثَ فِي ٱلۡأُمِّيِّۧنَ رَسُولٗا مِّنۡهُمۡ يَتۡلُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ وَيُزَكِّيهِمۡ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ وَإِن كَانُواْ مِن قَبۡلُ لَفِي ضَلَٰلٖ مُّبِينٖ ٢\nThe ultimate intent behind this Book [the Quran] is to have deep understanding and practice. It is to have knowledge that is revered by putting it into practice and actions that are perfected through the knowledge which is based on revelation and reason. With that, its followers place everything, firmly, where it belongs so that they do not deviate like the Children of Israel did and share their example of a donkey carrying books. If the Prophet (ﷺ) did not have any miracle except the Quran, it would still be considered the ultimate miracle. Al-Biqai: 20/51.\nWhen does a Muslim attain a complete benefit from the Quran?\nمَثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ حُمِّلُواْ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةَ ثُمَّ لَمۡ يَحۡمِلُوهَا كَمَثَلِ ٱلۡحِمَارِ يَحۡمِلُ أَسۡفَارَۢاۚ بِئۡسَ مَثَلُ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَذَّبُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِۚ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٥\nAllah admonishes the Jews who were entrusted with the Torah and ordered to adhere to it, but they did not, hence, Allah likens them to (a donkey who carries volumes of books). Surely, when the donkey carries books, it does not understand what these books contain because it is only carrying them physically. This is the example of those who were entrusted with the Torah; they memorized its words but did not understand their meanings, nor abided by them. Ibn Kathir: 4/364.\nFor one who memorizes the Quran, but does not understand, reflect or practice it, can he be considered among the people of the Quran?\nمَثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ حُمِّلُواْ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةَ ثُمَّ لَمۡ يَحۡمِلُوهَا كَمَثَلِ ٱلۡحِمَارِ يَحۡمِلُ أَسۡفَارَۢاۚ\nEven though this example is made about the Jews, its meaning may apply to those who learned the Quran, then neglected to practice its teachings, did not revere it, or observe it faithfully. Al-Qasimi: 9/22.\nDoes this example apply only to the people of the Torah?\nمَثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ حُمِّلُواْ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةَ ثُمَّ لَمۡ يَحۡمِلُوهَا كَمَثَلِ ٱلۡحِمَارِ يَحۡمِلُ أَسۡفَارَۢاۚ\nMaimun bin Mahran said: A donkey does not know what is carrying on its back: A book or trash, and so do the Jews. Al-Shawkani: 5/225.\nMaimun bin Mahran's statement likens Jews to a donkey. How?\nwords\nيُسَبِّحُExalting Allah above all that which is not suitable for Him\nالقُدُّوسِThe Most Holy, exalted above every deficiency\nالعَزِيزِThe All-Mighty\nالأُمِّيِّينَThe unlettered, the Arabs\nلَمَّا يَلحَقُوا بِهِمHave not yet joined them, but coming\nأَسفَارًاVolumes of books\nبِئسَ مَثَلُ القَومِWretched is their example"],[554,"§Al-Jumu'ah, Al-Munafiqun\ndeeds\nRemember Allah, the Almighty, often, glorify Him, and say: There is none worthy of worship but Allah.\nWhen the announcer calls to prayer, drop everything and head directly to the mosque.\nExplain to your family and friends the risk of the hypocrites and that they are enemies of Islam.\nguid\nRemembering Allah often is the way to success.\nLying is among the traits of hypocrites.\nDo not be deluded by appearances and forms, as the truth is what matters.\nrefl\nفَٱسۡعَوۡاْ إِلَىٰ ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِ وَذَرُواْ ٱلۡبَيۡعَۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡ إِن كُنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ٩\nI say: Mentioning (the remembrance of Allah) here rather than saying, \"to prayer\", as He says afterward: (And when the prayer has been concluded) to cover both: Al-Jumu’ah sermon and prayer. Ibn Ashur: 28/225.\nWhat is meant by (the remembrance of Allah) here?\nفَإِذَا قُضِيَتِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةُ فَٱنتَشِرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱبۡتَغُواْ مِن فَضۡلِ ٱللَّهِ\nIrak bin Malik (t) used to stand by the gate of the mosque and invoke Allah, saying, \"O Allah, I have accepted and complied with Your Call, performed the prayer that You ordained, and dispersed as You ordered me, so grant me of Your bounty and You are the best of providers.\" Ibn Kathir: 4/367.\nIrak bin Malik (t) put this verse into practice. How?\nفَإِذَا قُضِيَتِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةُ فَٱنتَشِرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱبۡتَغُواْ مِن فَضۡلِ ٱللَّهِ وَٱذۡكُرُواْ ٱللَّهَ كَثِيرٗا لَّعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ١٠\nSince focusing on trade is likely to make one forget to remember Allah, Allah instructs His servants to remember Him often. Al-Saadi: 863.\nAfter directing the believers to disperse and seek provision, the verse concludes with ordaining the remembrance of Allah. Why?\nوَإِذَا رَأَوۡاْ تِجَٰرَةً أَوۡ لَهۡوًا ٱنفَضُّوٓاْ إِلَيۡهَا وَتَرَكُوكَ قَآئِمٗاۚ قُلۡ مَا عِندَ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهۡوِ وَمِنَ ٱلتِّجَٰرَةِۚ وَٱللَّهُ خَيۡرُ ٱلرَّٰزِقِينَ ١١\nPatience in obeying Allah and continuing one's act of worship does not cause one to miss out on provision, for Allah is the best provider. So, whoever fears Allah, Allah will grant him provision from where he does not expect. Al-Saadi: 863.\nThis verse implies that righteousness is among the causes for provision. Explain.\nإِذَا جَآءَكَ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقُونَ قَالُواْ نَشۡهَدُ إِنَّكَ لَرَسُولُ ٱللَّهِۗ وَٱللَّهُ يَعۡلَمُ إِنَّكَ لَرَسُولُهُۥ وَٱللَّهُ يَشۡهَدُ إِنَّ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ لَكَٰذِبُونَ ١\nAllah testifies that the hypocrites are liars, even though their apparent statement is true, because their inward contradicts their outward, since deeds are judged only by intentions. Al-Shanqiti: 8/188.\nAllah testifies that the hypocrites are liars. Why?\n۞وَإِذَا رَأَيۡتَهُمۡ تُعۡجِبُكَ أَجۡسَامُهُمۡۖ وَإِن يَقُولُواْ تَسۡمَعۡ لِقَوۡلِهِمۡۖ كَأَنَّهُمۡ خُشُبٞ مُّسَنَّدَةٞۖ يَحۡسَبُونَ كُلَّ صَيۡحَةٍ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ هُمُ ٱلۡعَدُوُّ فَٱحۡذَرۡهُمۡۚ قَٰتَلَهُمُ ٱللَّهُۖ أَنَّىٰ يُؤۡفَكُونَ ٤\nThe outward appearance of the hypocrites is beautiful like planks of wood leaned against the wall. He likens them as such because they do not listen or reason, similar to ghosts without souls and bodies without minds. Moreover, it is said that they resemble decaying planks of wood of which the inside is unknown, and are leaning against something else. Al-Qurtubi: 20/500.\nAllah likens the hypocrites to planks of wood leaned against the wall. Why?\nهُمُ ٱلۡعَدُوُّ\nThey are the enemy in the true sense, because the enemy who is clearly and openly an enemy is easier to deal with than an unnoticeable enemy who resorts to trickery and deceit, and claims to be an ally when, in fact, he is an avowed enemy. Al-Saadi: 864.\nAllah describes the hypocrites as the enemy. Why?\nwords\nوَذَرُواLeave off\nانفَضُّوا إِلَيهَاThey rushed to it\nفَطُبِعَHave been sealed over\nكَأَنَّهُم خُشُبٌ مُسَنَّدَةٌThey are like planks of wood leaned against the wall because their hearts are devoid of faith\nكُلَّ صَيحَةٍ عَلَيهِمThey deem every cry to be against them because they feel insecure"],[555,"§Al-Munafiqun\ndeeds\nAttend an Islamic study circle or a lecture.\nSeek Allah's forgiveness for you and for the believing men and women.\nDonate to a charitable organization to sponsor a preacher or a student of Islamic studies to distance yourself from the traits of the hypocrites.\nguid\nAll honor belongs to Allah. Whoever seeks honor, should ask the One Who owns it.\nWealth and children may cause one to be distant from Allah.\nStrive to do good deeds so that you have a good end of life.\nrefl\nوَلِلَّهِ خَزَآئِنُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ لَا يَفۡقَهُونَ ٧\nAllah says, (but the hypocrites do not understand) to indicate their short-sightedness and uncertainty when they said: (Do not spend on those who are with Allah's Messenger so that they may desert him), assuming that ceasing to spend on those who were with Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) would make them disband. Their belief that the ability to spend is confined to them since they were wealthy, reflected their heedlessness of the means and causes of wealth and poverty. Ibn Ashur: 28/248.\nAllah says, (but the hypocrites do not understand). Why?\nوَلِلَّهِ ٱلۡعِزَّةُ وَلِرَسُولِهِۦ وَلِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٨\nPeople seek honor at the doorsteps of kings, but they will only find it in obeying Allah. Alhasan Al-Basri said: Those who disobey Allah will always be humiliated by Him for their sins, even if they appear to have the fastest and most beautiful procession. Ibn Taimyah: 6/312.\nWhere can real honor be found?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُلۡهِكُمۡ أَمۡوَٰلُكُمۡ وَلَآ أَوۡلَٰدُكُمۡ عَن ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nAfter Allah mentions the ugly traits of the hypocrites, He addresses the believers, encourages them to remember Him, and says, (O you who believe, do not let your wealth and your children distract you from Allah's remembrance). He warns them against the traits of the hypocrites who were distracted by their wealth and children from Allah's remembrance. Al-Shawkani: 5/233.\nWhat is the link between this verse and the one before?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُلۡهِكُمۡ أَمۡوَٰلُكُمۡ وَلَآ أَوۡلَٰدُكُمۡ عَن ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nAllah forbids the distraction from His remembrance by wealth and children because wealth keeps people busy thinking how to earn and increase it even more often than thinking about their children. Since thinking about earning, multiplying, and saving wealth distracts from the remembrance of Allah, it also distracts from His call for spending it. Ibn Ashur: 28/251.\nDistraction by wealth and children is singled out for prohibition. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُلۡهِكُمۡ أَمۡوَٰلُكُمۡ وَلَآ أَوۡلَٰدُكُمۡ عَن ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nConstant remembrance of Allah is a means for His love. Allah's remembrance to the heart is like water to the plant, without which the plant dies out. Allah's remembrance comes in many ways, first: Mentioning His Holy Names and Attributes, and praising Him by them. Second: Exalting Allah, praising Him, saying: Allah is the Greatest, saying: There is none worthy of worship but Allah, and glorifying Him; this is the most common remembrance of Allah practiced in later generations. Third: Remembering Allah by mentioning His rules, commands, and prohibitions; this is practiced by the scholars. Fourth: Remembering Allah by reciting His word, [the Quran]. Fifth: Remembering Allah by supplication, asking forgiveness, and invocation. These are five ways to remember Allah. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/157-158.\nShow the importance of Allah's remembrance, and state its ways.\nوَأَنفِقُواْ مِن مَّا رَزَقۡنَٰكُم\nThis highlights the fact that Allah does not burden people with spending that is beyond their means and is too difficult for them. Rather, He instructs them to spend some of what He has provided and made available to them. Al-Saadi: 865.\nThe preposition (from) serves a purpose in this verse. What is it?\nمِّن قَبۡلِ أَن يَأۡتِيَ أَحَدَكُمُ ٱلۡمَوۡتُ فَيَقُولَ رَبِّ لَوۡلَآ أَخَّرۡتَنِيٓ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ قَرِيبٖ فَأَصَّدَّقَ وَأَكُن مِّنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ١٠\nSurely, every person who fell into shortcomings will regret it at the time of his death and will ask for respite, even if it is a short period, so that he does better and attains what he missed. Ibn Kathir: 4/373.\nIs regret at the time of death limited to the disbelievers? What lesson we learned from this?\nwords\nلَوَّوا رُؤُوسَهُمThey turn their heads aside in arrogance\nيَصُدُّونَThey turn away\nيَنفَضُّواThey desert him\nرَجَعنَاWe return to Al-Madinah\nلاَ تُلهِكُمDo not be distracted\nلَولاَ أَخَّرتَنِيIf only You would give me respite\nأَجَلُهَاIts appointed time of death"],[556,"§At-Taghabun\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah just as you perfected my creation, also perfect my moral character.\"\nRead a story from the Quran about a people who were destroyed, and draw the reasons for their doom.\nAsk Allah to make the final days of your life the best ones ever.\nguid\nThe emphatic belief in what Allah has decreed for people is an essential part of faith.\nWhoever believes in the Resurrection, must work and be ready for that Day.\nAmong the names of the Day of Resurrection is the Day of great loss, because people will be separated as winners and losers.\nrefl\nيُسَبِّحُ لِلَّهِ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ لَهُ ٱلۡمُلۡكُ وَلَهُ ٱلۡحَمۡدُۖ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٌ ١\nThe praise of all creatures in the heavens and earth is to Allah because all of them receive goodness only from Him and none can provide provision for them except Him. Hence, all of their praise is due to Him. Al-Tabari: 23/415.\nThe praise of all creatures in the heavens and earth is to Allah. Why?\nخَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَصَوَّرَكُمۡ فَأَحۡسَنَ صُوَرَكُمۡۖ وَإِلَيۡهِ ٱلۡمَصِيرُ ٣\nIt is said that Allah created man in the best form among all creatures, as indicated by the fact that he does not wish for a different form out of what he sees around him. The beauty of his form is that he is created to stand upright, not facing downward. Al-Qurtubi: 21/9.\nWhat is meant by (and shaped you and perfected your forms)?\nوَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمُۢ بِذَاتِ ٱلصُّدُورِ ٤\nSince Allah knows well what is in our hearts, it is essential for the wise person to be keen and strive to guard his inner thoughts from bad attitudes, and to acquire good characteristics. Al-Saadi: 866.\nWhat is the benefit of knowing that Allah is All-Knowing of what is in the hearts?\nأَلَمۡ يَأۡتِكُمۡ نَبَؤُاْ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِن قَبۡلُ فَذَاقُواْ وَبَالَ أَمۡرِهِمۡ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٞ ٥\nAllah likens their punishment to something that tastes bad to be tasted and swallowed, for tasting by tongue is more intense than touching by hand or skin. Ibn Ashur: 28/268.\nAllah describes the disbelievers when taking the punishment as tasting. Why?\nزَعَمَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ أَن لَّن يُبۡعَثُواْۚ قُلۡ بَلَىٰ وَرَبِّي لَتُبۡعَثُنَّ ثُمَّ لَتُنَبَّؤُنَّ بِمَا عَمِلۡتُمۡۚ وَذَٰلِكَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ يَسِيرٞ ٧\nWhat is commonly considered \"difficult\" for people is never as such for Allah. Allah says, (And it is He who begins creation; then He repeats it, and that is easier for Him) [30:27]. Ibn Ashur: 28/272.\nThe verse describes the resurrection as (easy). Why?\nيَوۡمَ يَجۡمَعُكُمۡ لِيَوۡمِ ٱلۡجَمۡعِۖ ذَٰلِكَ يَوۡمُ ٱلتَّغَابُنِۗ\nThose who will lose their families and their dwellings in Paradise suffer a great loss. On that Day, the great loss of every disbeliever who neglected faith will manifest; moreover, every believer will feel a great loss for his shortcomings. Al-Alusi: 14/319.\nThe Day of Resurrection is called the Day of great loss. Why?\nيَوۡمَ يَجۡمَعُكُمۡ لِيَوۡمِ ٱلۡجَمۡعِۖ ذَٰلِكَ يَوۡمُ ٱلتَّغَابُنِۗ\n(The Day of great loss), the Day of Resurrection. The Arabic word, \"Taghabun\" is derived from when people trade with each other; a person's incurring loss in business and another's gaining a profit. So, when those who are destined for bliss enter Paradise, they will take over the dwellings of those who are wretched, which would have been theirs had they been of the believers. Ibn Juzay: 2/452.\nHow will the great loss occur on the Day of Resurrection?\nwords\nيُسَبِّحُExalting Allah above all that which is not suitable for Him\nالمَصِيرُThe final return\nوَبَالَ أَمرِهِمThe evil consequence of their disbelief\nوَتَوَلَّواTurned away from the truth\nوَالنُّورِThe light, the Quran\nلِيَومِ الجَمعِThe Day of Gathering, Resurrection\nيَومُ التَّغَابُنِThe Day of great loss\nيُكَفِّرExpiates"],[557,"§At-Taghabun\ndeeds\nGet together with your spouse and children, or some of your brothers, and study a verse from the Book of Allah.\nPardon a Muslim who erred against you, so that Allah may pardon you.\nGive money to charity, even a little, to overcome the trial of wealth.\nguid\nContentment with the divine decree and destiny is an essential part of faith.\nFaith makes the heart steadfast when calamity befalls.\nWhoever is protected from stinginess, becomes successful.\nrefl\nمَآ أَصَابَ مِن مُّصِيبَةٍ إِلَّا بِإِذۡنِ ٱللَّهِۗ وَمَن يُؤۡمِنۢ بِٱللَّهِ يَهۡدِ قَلۡبَهُ\nThis is general in meaning and includes all calamities. Everything that befalls people happens by the will and decree of Allah. What matters is whether the individual will do what is required of him or not. If he does what is required of him, then he will have a great reward in this world and the Hereafter. If he believes that it is from Allah, and he accepts it and submits to His decree, Allah will guide his heart, and he will be reassured and will not panic at times of calamity. Al-Saadi: 867.\nWhen you know that calamities are from Allah, what are the implications of that?\nوَمَن يُؤۡمِنۢ بِٱللَّهِ يَهۡدِ قَلۡبَهُۥۚ وَٱللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيۡءٍ عَلِيمٞ ١١\n(And whoever believes in Allah, He will guide his heart), Ibn Abbas said: It means that Allah will guide his heart to have certain faith, where he knows that what has come to him could not have missed him, and what has missed him could not have come to him. Al-Tabari: 23/42.\nWhat is meant by (He will guide his heart)?\nوَعَلَى ٱللَّهِ فَلۡيَتَوَكَّلِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ١٣\nDescribing them, here, as (believers) indicates the importance of belief for the reliance upon Allah, where the strength and weakness of reliance are commensurate with the level of faith in Allah. The greater the servant's belief in Allah, the stronger his reliance becomes, and the opposite is true. If his reliance is weak, that is a certain indication of his weak faith. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/15.\nAllah addresses them as (the believers) after enjoining them to rely upon Him. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِنَّ مِنۡ أَزۡوَٰجِكُمۡ وَأَوۡلَٰدِكُمۡ عَدُوّٗا لَّكُمۡ فَٱحۡذَرُوهُمۡۚ\nAbu Bakr bin Al-Arabi said: \"This clarifies the reason for enmity; where it is not an inherited enmity, rather, it is due to their actions.When a spouse or a son's actions are similar to that of an enemy, then, he becomes one, and there is no action more disgraceful than preventing a servant from disobeying Allah.\" Al-Qurtubi: 17/152.\nHow can a spouse or a son become an enemy?\nإِنَّمَآ أَمۡوَٰلُكُمۡ وَأَوۡلَٰدُكُمۡ فِتۡنَةٞۚ وَٱللَّهُ عِندَهُۥٓ أَجۡرٌ عَظِيمٞ ١٥\nIbn Masoud said: \"None of you should say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the trial, as every one of you already has one, because Allah says, (Your wealth and your children are but a trial); but if any of you seeks refuge, let him seek refuge with Allah from misleading trials.\" Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/160.\nWhat supplication should the person say when facing trials?\nفَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ مَا ٱسۡتَطَعۡتُمۡ\nHere, Allah commands His servants to fear Him, which means complying with His commands and heeding His prohibitions, according to what one is able to do. This verse indicates that every duty a person is unable to do because it is too difficult for him is waived in his case, but if he is able to do some of it and unable to do the rest, then he should do whatever he is capable of, and the rest will be waived for him. Al-Saadi: 86.\nWhat benefit will you gain by knowing that fearing Allah is required to the best of your ability?\nفَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ مَا ٱسۡتَطَعۡتُمۡ وَٱسۡمَعُواْ وَأَطِيعُواْ وَأَنفِقُواْ خَيۡرٗا لِّأَنفُسِكُمۡۗ وَمَن يُوقَ شُحَّ نَفۡسِهِۦ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُفۡلِحُونَ ١٦ إِن تُقۡرِضُواْ ٱللَّهَ قَرۡضًا حَسَنٗا يُضَٰعِفۡهُ لَكُمۡ وَيَغۡفِرۡ لَكُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ شَكُورٌ حَلِيمٌ ١٧\nThe aim here is to emphasize the virtue of spending for charity that is enjoined. It is described as: Better for the giver, a reason for success, and a goodly loan from the servant to his Lord. This is sufficient encouragement and graciousness in request by making the giver as if he were handing out money to Allah, the Almighty. It manifests the meaning of doing good with Allah. Ibn Ashur: 28/290.\nIn this verse, spending for charity is encouraged through many ways. What are they?\nwords\nبِإِذنِ اللهِBy the decree of Allah\nيَهدِ قَلبَهُHe will guide his heart to submission\nتَوَلَّيتُم(ﷺ) You turned away from obeying the Prophet\nفَليَتَوَكَّلِLet him rely\nتَعفُواYou pardon\nوَتَصفَحُواYou overlook"],[558,"§At-Talaq\ndeeds\nCaution a Muslim against transgressing the limits set by Allah.\nEnsure that you read the daily remembrance of Allah in the morning and evening, as it is a means of relying upon Allah.\nExplain to a friend of yours that fearing Allah is a means of provision, expiation of sins, and rising high in rank with Allah; while remembering this verse:\nguid\nIt is important to reflect on Sharia's aims and interests that result from the rules of divorce.\nIt is important to deal honorably in all matters, especially with those who are weak.\nFearing Allah is a way out of every hardship.\nrefl\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ رَبَّكُمۡۖ لَا تُخۡرِجُوهُنَّ مِنۢ بُيُوتِهِنَّ وَلَا يَخۡرُجۡنَ إِلَّآ أَن يَأۡتِينَ بِفَٰحِشَةٖ مُّبَيِّنَةٖۚ\n(And fear Allah, your Lord), this is a warning against taking lightly the rules of divorce and waiting period, as the people during the times of ignorance did not care much for women, and the relatives of a divorced woman seldom come to her defense. Hence, people neglected and violated women's rights. That is why these verses give a stern challenge, and express observing these rights as fearing Allah and as limits set by Him. Moreover, the use of Allah's name, (your Lord) is a reminder to evade His wrath. Ibn Ashur: 28/298-299.\nWhat is the benefit of mentioning the fear of Allah among the rules of divorce?\nذَٰلِكُمۡ يُوعَظُ بِهِۦ مَن كَانَ يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِۚ وَمَن يَتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ يَجۡعَل لَّهُۥ مَخۡرَجٗا ٢\nThose who believe in Allah and the Last Day are singled out for mention because they are the only ones who benefit from this exhortation. Al-Shawkani: 5/241.\nThose who believe in Allah and the Last Day are singled out for this exhortation. Why?\nوَمَن يَتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ يَجۡعَل لَّهُۥ مَخۡرَجٗا ٢\nWhoever does not fear Allah will face difficulties, obstacles, and troubles that he cannot find a way out of or escape the consequences thereof. This is also applicable to divorce. If a person does not fear Allah with regard to the rulings of divorce, and issues a divorce in a prohibited manner, such as issuing the threefold divorce and the like, he will inevitably come to regret it and will not be able to escape the negative consequences thereof. Al-Saadi: 870.\nFor one who does not have fear of Allah, how does he deal with difficulties and disasters?\nوَمَن يَتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ يَجۡعَل لَّهُۥ مَخۡرَجٗا ٢\n(He will make a way out for him), Ibn Abbas said: Allah will save him from every distress in this life and the Hereafter. It is said that (a way out) means Allah makes him content with what He had given him. Al-Kalbi said: Allah will make for him a way out of the Fire to Paradise. Al-Rabi bin Khuthaym [said]: Allah will make a way out from everything that distresses people. Al-Qurtubi: 21/42-43.\nWhat is meant by (a way out) in this verse?\nوَيَرۡزُقۡهُ مِنۡ حَيۡثُ لَا يَحۡتَسِبُۚ\nSome scholars said: There are two types of provisions, first: An assured provision for every being throughout his life, that is, the sustenance (food) by which his living continues, and it is indicated by the verse, (There is no moving creature on earth but upon Allah is its provision)[11:6]. Second: A promised provision only for those who fear Allah, which is mentioned in this verse. Ibn Juzay: 2/456.\nTwo types of provisions are inferred from this verse. What are they?\nوَمَن يَتَوَكَّلۡ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ فَهُوَ حَسۡبُهُۥٓۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بَٰلِغُ أَمۡرِهِۦۚ قَدۡ جَعَلَ ٱللَّهُ لِكُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدۡرٗا ٣\nWhen Allah mentions His sufficiency for those who rely on Him, some may assume His immediate sufficiency right at the time of their reliance, therefore, He followed that by saying: (For Allah has set a destiny for everything), which means a set time that cannot be extended, and Allah brings it at the appointed time that He decreed. Hence, the one who relies upon Allah must not seek to hasten the result by saying: I have relied on Allah and supplicated Him, but did not see anything, nor have I been sufficed. Allah will surely accomplish His purpose at the appointed time that He decreed. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/165.\nThis verse ends with (For Allah has set a destiny for everything). Why?\nذَٰلِكَ أَمۡرُ ٱللَّهِ أَنزَلَهُۥٓ إِلَيۡكُمۡۚ وَمَن يَتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ يُكَفِّرۡ عَنۡهُ سَيِّـَٔاتِهِۦ وَيُعۡظِمۡ لَهُۥٓ أَجۡرًا ٥\n(And will reward him immensely), Allah will reward him greatly for his deeds and righteousness, by admitting him into Paradise, abiding therein forever. Al-Tabari: 23/456.\nExplain how Allah, the Almighty, will immensely reward those who fear Him .\nwords\nفَطَلِّقُوهُنَّ لِعِدَّتِهِنَّDivorce them after the completion of their periods but before sexual intercourse\nوَأَقِيمُواEstablish, give true testimony\nبَالِغُ أَمرِهِAllah will surely accomplish His purpose\nقَدرًاA destiny\nيَئِسنَWomen who reached their menopause\nارتَبتُمIf you doubt, did not know the ruling"],[559,"§At-Talaq\ndeeds\nForbid something wrong today.\nAsk Allah for guidance and piety.\nRecite verses from the Quran to some of your brethren and relatives.\nguid\nCausing harm and annoyance to others is prohibited.\nReflecting on the punishments of those who were insolent and arrogant.\nDo good deeds which is within your capacity.\nrefl\nفَإِنۡ أَرۡضَعۡنَ لَكُمۡ فَـَٔاتُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ وَأۡتَمِرُواْ بَيۡنَكُم بِمَعۡرُوفٖۖ\nThe Arabic word for (graciously) is in indefinite form to indicate that they should be satisfied with what is feasible, which is dealing with people in fairness, dealing with oneself in denial, and dealing with the truth by acceptance. Al-Biqai: 20/161.\nThe Arabic word for (graciously) is in indefinite form. Why?\nوَأۡتَمِرُواْ بَيۡنَكُم بِمَعۡرُوفٖۖ وَإِن تَعَاسَرۡتُمۡ فَسَتُرۡضِعُ لَهُۥٓ أُخۡرَىٰ ٦\nGracious settlement implies that common tradition is relevant in this case, and it is a plain caution against harming either parent through his/her child. Moreover, all matters should be settled, after separation, through mutual understanding, and that includes breastfeeding and other matters. The settling of all matters should be based on graciousness, tolerance, and kindness for the sake of old times, and do not forget graciousness between you. Al-Shanqiti: 8/216.\nAn Islamic etiquette that should be observed after the divorce, what is it?\nلِيُنفِقۡ ذُو سَعَةٖ مِّن سَعَتِهِۦۖ وَمَن قُدِرَ عَلَيۡهِ رِزۡقُهُۥ فَلۡيُنفِقۡ مِمَّآ ءَاتَىٰهُ ٱللَّهُۚ لَا يُكَلِّفُ ٱللَّهُ نَفۡسًا إِلَّا مَآ ءَاتَىٰهَاۚ سَيَجۡعَلُ ٱللَّهُ بَعۡدَ عُسۡرٖ يُسۡرٗا ٧\n(Let the wealthy man spend according to his means), each one should spend according to his means in a balanced way where the husband is not overburdened and the wife is not neglected. This verse proves that spending varies according to people's capabilities. Ibn Juzay: 2/459.\nThis verse demonstrates an aspect of mitigating difficulties. Explain.\nوَكَأَيِّن مِّن قَرۡيَةٍ عَتَتۡ عَنۡ أَمۡرِ رَبِّهَا وَرُسُلِهِۦ فَحَاسَبۡنَٰهَا حِسَابٗا شَدِيدٗا وَعَذَّبۡنَٰهَا عَذَابٗا نُّكۡرٗا ٨ فَذَاقَتۡ وَبَالَ أَمۡرِهَا وَكَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ أَمۡرِهَا خُسۡرًا ٩\nHe who sows thrones will not harvest roses. Whoever neglected his duty toward Allah, will not have his rights protected, and whoever is burned by disobeying Allah, let him bear the harshness of His punishment. Al-Biqai: 20/167.\nWhat is the punishment of a city or a community when they turn away from the command of their Lord?\nوَكَأَيِّن مِّن قَرۡيَةٍ عَتَتۡ عَنۡ أَمۡرِ رَبِّهَا وَرُسُلِهِۦ فَحَاسَبۡنَٰهَا حِسَابٗا شَدِيدٗا وَعَذَّبۡنَٰهَا عَذَابٗا نُّكۡرٗا ٨ فَذَاقَتۡ وَبَالَ أَمۡرِهَا وَكَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ أَمۡرِهَا خُسۡرًا ٩\nMeaning: We took its inhabitants to sever account. It is said that it means that will be the reckoning and punishment in the Hereafter. It is, also, said that it was in this life, which is more probable, because the punishment in the Hereafter is mentioned after that in saying: (Allah has prepared for them a severe punishment), or because the verbs (We took it) and (and punished it) are in the past tense, which means: We took them to account for their sins and none of their minor sins was forgiven. (Punishment) was their recompense in this worldly life, and (terrible) with an unprecedented intensity. Ibn Juzay: 2/459.\nWhen does punishing disobedient cities occur?\nفَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ يَٰٓأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْۚ\nMeaning: O people of mature thinking who understand the verses and exhortations of Allah, and realize that the One Who destroyed the past nations for their disbelief is also able to punish later nations; there is no difference between them and those who come after them. Al-Saadi: 872.\nThe command to fear Allah is mentioned after relating the story of a doomed city. Why?\nٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ سَبۡعَ سَمَٰوَٰتٖ وَمِنَ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ مِثۡلَهُنَّۖ يَتَنَزَّلُ ٱلۡأَمۡرُ بَيۡنَهُنَّ\n(His command descends among them): Those who work with semantics said: His wonderous disposition of the affairs in heavens and earth. He sends down the rain to bring forth plants, and He brings the night and day, and summer and winter. He creates different animals, and changes them from one state into another. Al-Baghawi: 4/422.\nWhat is meant by (His command descends among them)?\nwords\nمِن وُجدِكُمIn accordance with your means\nأُولاَتِThey are\nوَأتَمِرُواConfer among yourselves\nبِمَعرُوفٍIn a graceful way\nتَعَاسَرتُمIf you are in discord over breastfeeding\nقُدِرَOne whose provision is restricted\nعَتَتRebelled and disobeyed\nوَبَالَ أَمرِهَاThe evil consequence of their deeds"],[560,"§At-Tahrim\ndeeds\nWrite an article or a message in which you make clear that sins are the causes of family problems. [\nFast for a day in the cause of Allah.\nAdvise your family with a message intended to protect them from the Hellfire.\nguid\nWhen gently reproaching someone, do not confront him with everything he did, lest he despair.\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) is always honored and protected by Allah.\nOverlooking some mistakes by your brethren indicates your generous nature.\nrefl\nقَدۡ فَرَضَ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡ تَحِلَّةَ أَيۡمَٰنِكُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ مَوۡلَىٰكُمۡۖ وَهُوَ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ٢\n(The All-Knowing), He knows what sets you right and ordains it for you. (The All-Wise): He has perfect actions and ordinances, hence, He does not enjoin nor forbid except what His wisdom entails. Al-Alusi: 14/345.\nThe verse ends with (The All-Knowing) and (The All-Wise). Why?\nوَإِذۡ أَسَرَّ ٱلنَّبِيُّ إِلَىٰ بَعۡضِ أَزۡوَٰجِهِۦ حَدِيثٗا\nThis verse was taken as evidence that it is permitted to confide a statement to a trustworthy wife or a friend and that they must keep it confidential. Al-Alusi: 14/346.\nWhat is the Sharia's ruling concerning confiding a statement, if it is right?\nوَإِذۡ أَسَرَّ ٱلنَّبِيُّ إِلَىٰ بَعۡضِ أَزۡوَٰجِهِۦ حَدِيثٗا فَلَمَّا نَبَّأَتۡ بِهِۦ وَأَظۡهَرَهُ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِ عَرَّفَ بَعۡضَهُۥ وَأَعۡرَضَ عَنۢ بَعۡضٖۖ\nWithholding some of the gentle reproach may increase the self-respect of the reproached person, and help him repent and not do it again. (And ignored a part): The Prophet (ﷺ) ignored the part on the female slave and honey graciously to avoid increasing reproaching, and a show of self-respect and kindness. Alhasan said: An honorable person never fully gets what is rightfully his. Sufyan Al-Thawri said: Overlooking is a trait of the great ones. Al-Biqai: 20/186.\nWhat is the useful lesson learned from: (He made known part of it and ignored a part)?\nوَأَعۡرَضَ عَنۢ بَعۡضٖۖ\nThe Prophet's (ﷺ) perfect good morals were manifested in Ignoring to make known a part of the statement to his wife. Sufyan said: Overlooking is a trait of the honorable ones. Alhasan said: An honorable person never gets fully what is rightfully his. When reproaching is overdone, it becomes a rebuke. Ibn Ashur: 28/353.\nOverlooking is a trait of the honorable ones. Explain in light of: (And ignored a part)?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ قُوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمۡ وَأَهۡلِيكُمۡ نَارٗا\nIbn Abbas (k) said: Refrain from what is forbidden by Allah and obey Him. Meaning: Command them [families] to do good deeds, forbid them from evil deeds, teach, and discipline them. Al-Baghawi: 4/430.\nHow can one protect himself and family from the Fire?\nنَارٗا وَقُودُهَا ٱلنَّاسُ وَٱلۡحِجَارَةُ عَلَيۡهَا مَلَٰٓئِكَةٌ غِلَاظٞ شِدَادٞ لَّا يَعۡصُونَ ٱللَّهَ مَآ أَمَرَهُمۡ وَيَفۡعَلُونَ مَا يُؤۡمَرُونَ ٦\nAllah describes the Fire in these terms to deter His servants from being heedless with regard to His commands. Al-Saadi: 874.\nWhy does Allah describe the fire in these terms?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ قُوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمۡ وَأَهۡلِيكُمۡ نَارٗا وَقُودُهَا ٱلنَّاسُ وَٱلۡحِجَارَةُ عَلَيۡهَا مَلَٰٓئِكَةٌ غِلَاظٞ شِدَادٞ لَّا يَعۡصُونَ ٱللَّهَ مَآ أَمَرَهُمۡ وَيَفۡعَلُونَ مَا يُؤۡمَرُونَ ٦ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَا تَعۡتَذِرُواْ ٱلۡيَوۡمَۖ إِنَّمَا تُجۡزَوۡنَ مَا كُنتُمۡ تَعۡمَلُونَ ٧\nThe Muslim Ummah is commanded by Allah to revere the Prophet (ﷺ), and therefore, any intentional abuse toward the Prophet (ﷺ) puts one beyond the pale of Islam. (O you who disbelieve) implies those who abused the Prophet (ﷺ), which, in turn, led to their abuse toward Allah and the people. Al-Biqai: 20/199.\nWhat is the Sharia's ruling on intentional abuse toward the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nwords\nتَحِلَّةَ أَيمَانِكُمAbsolving yourselves from your oaths\nمَولاَكُمYour helper and protector\nبَعضِ أَزوَاجِهِHafsa bint Omar (k)\nوَأَظهَرَهُAllah showed it to him\nعَرَّفَ بَعضَهُHe made known part of it to Hafsa (i)\nصَغَت قُلُوبُكُمَاYour hearts inclined toward liking what the Prophet disliked of making his secret known\nسَائِحَاتٍFasting women"],[561,"§At-Tahrim\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to accept your sincere repentance.\nInvoke Allah to lighten your heart and forgive you.\nPray two voluntary Rak'as and take your time.\nguid\nExert effort in striving against the disbelievers and the hypocrites and being harsh with them.\nBeing close to the righteous will not avail one unless he does righteous deeds.\nBe keen to supplicate Allah during times of trials.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ تُوبُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ تَوۡبَةٗ نَّصُوحًا\nAl-Qarthi said: A sincere repentance consists of four things: Asking forgiveness by words, ceasing the sins physically, intending by heart not to go back to sins, and abandoning evil company. Al-Baghawi: 4/430-431.\nWhat is the sincere repentance?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ جَٰهِدِ ٱلۡكُفَّارَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ وَٱغۡلُظۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ\nIt is well known that the hypocrites are disbelievers, and the Prophet's (ﷺ) Jihad against the disbelievers was by the sword, yet against the hypocrites it was by the Quran, as it was narrated in the Prophet's hadith: \"Lest people say that Muhammad is killing his Companions.\" Jihad by the Quran against the hypocrites was not less intense for them than the sword, because they were in constant fear, thinking that every shout was against them, their hearts became devoid, and they were like planks of wood leaned against the wall. This was harder for them than facing the sword, and Allah knows best. Al-Shanqiti: 8/223.\nExplain the difference between Jihad against the disbelievers and that against the hypocrites.\nضَرَبَ ٱللَّهُ مَثَلٗا لِّلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ ٱمۡرَأَتَ نُوحٖ وَٱمۡرَأَتَ لُوطٖۖ كَانَتَا تَحۡتَ عَبۡدَيۡنِ مِنۡ عِبَادِنَا صَٰلِحَيۡنِ فَخَانَتَاهُمَا فَلَمۡ يُغۡنِيَا عَنۡهُمَا مِنَ ٱللَّهِ شَيۡـٔٗا وَقِيلَ ٱدۡخُلَا ٱلنَّارَ مَعَ ٱلدَّٰخِلِينَ ١٠\nThis example is made to alert people that blood and kinship ties will not avail anyone when they are separated by faith in the Hereafter. Al-Qurtubi: 21/102.\nWhat is the aim of making this example?\nوَضَرَبَ ٱللَّهُ مَثَلٗا لِّلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱمۡرَأَتَ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِذۡ قَالَتۡ رَبِّ ٱبۡنِ لِي عِندَكَ بَيۡتٗا فِي ٱلۡجَنَّةِ\nThe scholars said: She chose the neighbor before the house. Ibn Kathir: 4/394.\nThe wife of Pharaoh said: (Near You) before saying: (A house). Why?\nوَنَجِّنِي مِن فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَعَمَلِهِۦ وَنَجِّنِي مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١١\nThis verse proves that seeking refuge with Allah and asking Him for salvation during times of trials and tribulations is among the ways of the righteous and Sunnah of the Prophets. This occurs often in the Quran. Al-Alusi: 14/358.\nThis verse contains one of the traits of the righteous. What is it?\nwords\nتَوبَةً نَصُوحًاSincere repentance\nلاَ يُخزِيHe will not disgrace nor punish\nوَاغلُظ عَلَيهِمBe harsh with them\nفَخَانَتَاهُمَاThey betrayed them\nأَحصَنَتShe guarded her chastity\nالقَانِتِينَThe devoutly obedient"],[562,"§Al-Mulk\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, make my deeds righteous and sincere to You.\" Then follow the Sunnah in every action you do.\nReflect on the creation of the stars, then thank Allah that He has forbidden the devils from eavesdropping, lest they mislead the people.\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask You to grant me fear of You in private and in public.\"\nguid\nEnsure to read Surat Al-Mulk every night.\nGlorify Allah in every matter.\nThose who refuse to obey the Prophets will face serious consequences, as Allah has prepared a grave punishment and rebuke to them.\nrefl\nتَبَٰرَكَ ٱلَّذِي بِيَدِهِ ٱلۡمُلۡكُ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٌ ١\nAllah governs all affairs; He sets forth what He wills with His Power while nothing can prevent Him, and to Him, there is no equivalent. Al-Biqai: 20/217.\nThe hearts find tranquility in relying upon Allah. Why?\nٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ ٱلۡمَوۡتَ وَٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ لِيَبۡلُوَكُمۡ أَيُّكُمۡ أَحۡسَنُ عَمَلٗاۚ وَهُوَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٢\n(Best in deeds): Fudhail bin Iyadh said: A correct and sincere deed. Deeds will not be accepted unless they are correct and sincere. Al-Baghawi: 4/435\nWhat is the meant by (Best in deeds)?\nثُمَّ ٱرۡجِعِ ٱلۡبَصَرَ كَرَّتَيۡنِ يَنقَلِبۡ إِلَيۡكَ ٱلۡبَصَرُ خَاسِئٗا وَهُوَ حَسِيرٞ ٤\nIt was commanded to look twice, because when a person looks at something once, he does not see its defect unless he looks at it again. Al-Qurtubi: 21/116.\nWhy is it commanded to look up at the heavens again?\nوَلَقَدۡ زَيَّنَّا ٱلسَّمَآءَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا بِمَصَٰبِيحَ وَجَعَلۡنَٰهَا رُجُومٗا لِّلشَّيَٰطِينِۖ وَأَعۡتَدۡنَا لَهُمۡ عَذَابَ ٱلسَّعِيرِ ٥\nQatadah said: Allah created stars for three purposes: Adornment of the heavens, missiles to stone the devils, and a compass to navigate the Earth. Ibn Juzay: 2/494.\nList the benefits of stars.\nتَكَادُ تَمَيَّزُ مِنَ ٱلۡغَيۡظِۖ كُلَّمَآ أُلۡقِيَ فِيهَا فَوۡجٞ سَأَلَهُمۡ خَزَنَتُهَآ أَلَمۡ يَأۡتِكُمۡ نَذِيرٞ ٨\nThis verse proves that Allah does not punish anyone with Fire unless warned beforehand in this worldly life. Al-Shanqiti: 8/233.\nWhat is indicated by the question: (Did there not come to you a warner?) by the keepers of the Hellfire to its dwellers?\nوَقَالُواْ لَوۡ كُنَّا نَسۡمَعُ أَوۡ نَعۡقِلُ مَا كُنَّا فِيٓ أَصۡحَٰبِ ٱلسَّعِيرِ ١٠\nThe mention of hearing precedes that of reason because those who are warned receive the call of the warner first, and then use reason to reflect on it. Ibn Ashur: 29/28.\nThe mention of hearing precedes that of reason. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخۡشَوۡنَ رَبَّهُم بِٱلۡغَيۡبِ لَهُم مَّغۡفِرَةٞ وَأَجۡرٞ كَبِيرٞ ١٢\nThe mention of forgiveness takes precedence as reassurance to their hearts because they fear accountability for their disbelief before Islam, minor sins and the like. Then, it is followed by good tidings of great reward, thus the statement follows the rule that says: Purification of the soul comes before beautification. Ibn Ashur: 29/29.\nIn this verse, the mention of forgiveness precedes that of the great reward. Why?\nwords\nطِبَاقًاOn top of each other without touching\nفُطُورٍRifts, cracks\nخَاسِئًاHumbled\nحَسِيرٌWeary\nرُجُومًا لِلشَّيَاطِينِMissiles to stone the devils who dare to eavesdrop\nشَهِيقًاDreadful inhale"],[563,"§Al-Mulk\ndeeds\nReflect on how Allah has flattened this Earth to walk on, then thank Him for His blessings.\nReflect on Allah's creation of birds' ability to fly above the earth and not fall, then say: \"Glory be to the One Who gave everything its form and then guided it.\"\n. Say, \"O Allah! let us enjoy our hearing, our sight and our power as long as You keep us alive.\" Then, thank Allah for them.\nguid\nThe path of righteousness and the path of falsehood are not equal.\nThe believer should not concern himself with trying to know the time of the Day of Resurrection but should get ready for it.\nAttribute all knowledge to Allah.\nrefl\nوَأَسِرُّواْ قَوۡلَكُمۡ أَوِ ٱجۡهَرُواْ بِهِۦٓۖ إِنَّهُۥ عَلِيمُۢ بِذَاتِ ٱلصُّدُورِ ١٣\nThat includes intentions and wills, let alone words and actions that are heard and seen. Al-Saadi: 876.\nThis verse concludes by declaring that Allah is All-Knowing. Why?\nأَلَا يَعۡلَمُ مَنۡ خَلَقَ وَهُوَ ٱللَّطِيفُ ٱلۡخَبِيرُ ١٤\nAllah concludes the argument with two Holy Names that reaffirm His argument, which are: the Most Subtle: The One Whose creation and wisdom are so subtle that they are beyond comprehension. The All-Aware: Whose knowledge encompasses all things, hidden and apparent. How can anything contained in the souls and concealed in the hearts be hidden from the Most Subtle, the All-Aware? Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/173.\nThis verse ends with Allah's Holy Names: (The Most Subtle) and (The All-Aware). Why?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ ذَلُولٗا فَٱمۡشُواْ فِي مَنَاكِبِهَا وَكُلُواْ مِن رِّزۡقِهِۦۖ وَإِلَيۡهِ ٱلنُّشُورُ ١٥\nAnd know that your efforts will not benefit you unless Allah makes matters easy for you. Allah continues to say, (and eat from His provision) Thus, striving by using the means to an end does not negate the necessity of relying upon Allah. Ibn Kathir: 4/398.\nWhat is indicated by adding “provisions” to the pronoun referring to Allah, the Almighty?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ ذَلُولٗا فَٱمۡشُواْ فِي مَنَاكِبِهَا وَكُلُواْ مِن رِّزۡقِهِۦۖ وَإِلَيۡهِ ٱلنُّشُورُ ١٥\nThe verse (And to Him is the resurrection) is a reminder that we are neither settlers nor inhabitants of this Earth, but have been placed in this world as wayfarers. As such, we must not live as if it is our permanent settlement. We are here to work for our life in the Hereafter; this life is nothing but a mere passage, not a permanent dwelling. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/174.\nThis verse enjoins making use of this earth, then, it mentions the resurrection. Why?\nءَأَمِنتُم مَّن فِي ٱلسَّمَآءِ أَن يَخۡسِفَ بِكُمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ فَإِذَا هِيَ تَمُورُ ١٦\nThe threat of the swallowing of the earth is mentioned before the threat of a storm of stones, because the former is one of the conditions of the earth, and talking about its conditions is closer here. Moreover, sending a storm of stones against them is a punishment for being ungrateful for Allah's blessings from which their earthly provisions come, which is indicated by this verse: (and eat from His provision), as the origins of earthly provisions are caused by the rains of heaven, as Allah says, (And in the heaven is your provision)[51:22]. Ibn Ashur: 29/36.\nWhy was the threat of the swallowing of the earth given precedence over the threat of the a storm of stones?\nأَفَمَن يَمۡشِي مُكِبًّا عَلَىٰ وَجۡهِهِۦٓ أَهۡدَىٰٓ أَمَّن يَمۡشِي سَوِيًّا عَلَىٰ صِرَٰطٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٖ ٢٢\nAllah sets an example for the believer and the disbeliever: (One who walks fallen on his face) with his head bowed down, looking neither in front of him nor to his right nor his left, so he is not safe from stumbling and falling on his face. Unlike the believer, who walks straight upright, looking at what is in front of him, what is on his right and his left. Al-Qurtubi: 21/129.\nFor whom does Allah set this example?\nقُلۡ هُوَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَنشَأَكُمۡ وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلسَّمۡعَ وَٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرَ وَٱلۡأَفۡـِٔدَةَۚ قَلِيلٗا مَّا تَشۡكُرُونَ ٢٣\n(Little do you give thanks), how little you use these abilities that Allah has blessed you with to obey Him, to act according to His commandments, and to avoid His prohibitions. Ibn Kathir: 4/399.\nWhat is indicated by concluding the verse by saying: (Little do you give thanks)?\nwords\nذَلُولًاSubservient, stable\nمَنَاكِبِهَاIts regions\nتَمُورُIt quakes\nحَاصِبًاA storm of stones\nلَجُّواPersisted\nوَنُفُورAversion"],[564,"§Al-Mulk, Al-Qalam\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to send the rain.\nIdentify three blessings that Allah has bestowed on you, and thank Him for them.\nSay, \"O Allah, guide me to the best of morals.\"\nguid\nEncourage upholding high morals.\nWoe to the liar, mocker, and backslider.\nWarning against compromising Allah's religion.\nrefl\nءَامَنَّا بِهِۦ وَعَلَيۡهِ تَوَكَّلۡنَاۖ\nBelief includes affirmation of the heart, and inward and outward deeds. Since carrying out deeds and perfecting them depends on reliance upon Allah, Allah singles out reliance on Him among all other deeds, which would otherwise be included in faith and its requirements. Al-Saadi: 878.\nAmong all deeds, Allah singles out reliance on Him, even though it is part of faith. Why?\nقُلۡ هُوَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ ءَامَنَّا بِهِۦ وَعَلَيۡهِ تَوَكَّلۡنَاۖ فَسَتَعۡلَمُونَ مَنۡ هُوَ فِي ضَلَٰلٖ مُّبِينٖ ٢٩\n(And upon Him), on Allah alone. (We have relied) because there is nothing in anyone's hands but His. Otherwise, those whom He wants to punish may be shown mercy, and those whom He wants to show mercy to may be punished. Hence, every mercy or punishment is solely from Him. Al-Biqai: 20/270.\nWhy do we solely rely on Allah?\nنٓۚ وَٱلۡقَلَمِ وَمَا يَسۡطُرُونَ ١\nSwearing by the pen stems from the honor of writing the holy Quran and other holy books, and books of education, high morality, and sciences. All of which is honorable with Allah, the Almighty. Ibn Ashur: 29/60.\nAllah swears by the pen. Why?\nإِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَن ضَلَّ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦ وَهُوَ أَعۡلَمُ بِٱلۡمُهۡتَدِينَ ٧\nThis is a threat to those who have gone astray and a promise to those who follow true guidance. Al-Saadi: 879.\nWhat is the benefit of mentioning Allah's knowledge of the strayed and the guided?\nفَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلۡمُكَذِّبِينَ ٨\nThe prohibition of obeying someone entails a prohibition of imitating him in the first place. Therefore, the liar and the swearer must not be obeyed or imitated. Ibn Taimyah: 6/370.\nThe verse indicates that it is forbidden to imitate people of immorality and corruption. Explain.\nفَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلۡمُكَذِّبِينَ ٨ وَدُّواْ لَوۡ تُدۡهِنُ فَيُدۡهِنُونَ ٩ وَلَا تُطِعۡ كُلَّ حَلَّافٖ مَّهِينٍ ١٠ هَمَّازٖ مَّشَّآءِۢ بِنَمِيمٖ ١١ مَّنَّاعٖ لِّلۡخَيۡرِ مُعۡتَدٍ أَثِيمٍ ١٢ عُتُلِّۢ بَعۡدَ ذَٰلِكَ زَنِيمٍ ١٣\nQualities are acquired through socializing, hence there is a warning about acquiring some of their morals through interacting with them. One has to be careful when interacting with them to call them to the way of Allah. Ibn Taimyah: 6/370.\nCalling the people of disobedience to the way of Allah comes with a warning, what is it?\nوَلَا تُطِعۡ كُلَّ حَلَّافٖ مَّهِينٍ ١٠\nThat is, due to the liar's weak character and lowliness; he protects himself by daring to swear falsely in the Names of Allah, which he uses all the time and out of place. Ibn Kathir: 4/404.\nWhy are we prohibited to obey those who swear often?\nwords\nرَأَوهُ زُلفَةًWhen they see the torment approaching\nتَدَّعُونَMockingly calling to hasten it\nيُجِيرُProtect\nغَورًاTo sink deep into the ground\nمَمنُونٍInterrupted\nتُدهِنُCompromise\nهَمَّازٍBackbiter\nعُتُلٍّCruel, wicked disbeliever\nزَنِيمٍIllegitimate child"],[565,"§Al-Qalam\ndeeds\nGive charity to a needy person.\nSay, \"None has the right to be worshiped except You. Glory be to You! I have been of the wrongdoers.\"\nPray two Rak'a and prostrate long, then ask Allah to make good your standing before Him in judgment.\nguid\nThis worldly life is a place of trials and tribulations.\nAdmission of guilt is the first step to salvation.\nSensing the great punishment for the deniers, and the great bliss for the righteous.\nrefl\nإِنَّا بَلَوۡنَٰهُمۡ كَمَا بَلَوۡنَآ أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلۡجَنَّةِ\nWe have tested these people, who deny the truth, and We have given them respite and bestowed upon them whatever We willed of wealth, children, long life, and akin to it, which coincided with their wishes, not because they are dear to Us, but so that they may be gradually led to their ruin in ways they do not perceive. Al-Saadi: 880.\nIs wealth or poverty a sign of Allah's love for the rich and dislike for the poor?\nفَطَافَ عَلَيۡهَا طَآئِفٞ مِّن رَّبِّكَ وَهُمۡ نَآئِمُونَ ١٩\nAllah punished them before their actual prevention of charity because they were firm on depriving the poor of the fruits, and swore to cut them early, which was an actual prevention of charity. There is a lesson in this for those who withhold their wealth from consoling the needy. Ibn Ashur: 29/82.\nAllah punished them before their actual prevention of charity. Why?\nوَغَدَوۡاْ عَلَىٰ حَرۡدٖ قَٰدِرِينَ ٢٥\nThey were able to give fruits to the poor, but they intended to prevent and deprive them of it. Then, they became in a situation where they were unable to do anything except deprivation. Al-Alusi: 15/36.\nThe people of the garden were hastily deprived of their garden. Why?\nبَلۡ نَحۡنُ مَحۡرُومُونَ ٢٧\nMeaning: We were deprived of the garden's fruits and goodness because we kept it from the poor, and for not saying: \"If Allah wills.\" Al-Baghawi: 4/451.\nThe people of the garden were deprived of goodness. Why?\nقَالَ أَوۡسَطُهُمۡ أَلَمۡ أَقُل لَّكُمۡ لَوۡلَا تُسَبِّحُونَ ٢٨\n(The middle one of them), the best one and closer to righteousness among them, and he was one of three brothers. In Arabic, the term, (middle) refers to the best. Allah says, (And thus We have made you a middle nation)[2:143], and (Be mindful of the prayers, especially the middle prayer)[2:238]. Ibn Ashur: 29/86.\nThe middle brother was singled out for mention. Why?\nإِنَّ لِلۡمُتَّقِينَ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ٣٤\n(With their Lord), this indicates that Allah is pleased with them, and the pleasure of the Lord of the house is needed before seeing the house. Al-Biqai: 20/317.\nWhat is indicated by (With their Lord)?\nيَوۡمَ يُكۡشَفُ عَن سَاقٖ وَيُدۡعَوۡنَ إِلَى ٱلسُّجُودِ فَلَا يَسۡتَطِيعُونَ ٤٢\nThey will be punished with the opposite of what they did. When they were called to prostrate in the worldly life, they refused to do so, even though they were healthy and secure. Therefore, they will be punished with the lack of ability to do so in the Hereafter. When the Almighty Lord makes Himself visible (before the believers), then the believers will fall down in prostration to Him, but no one of the disbelievers and hypocrites will be able to prostrate. Rather, their backs will become one plate. Ibn Kathir: 4/407.\nWhy will they be prevented from prostration on that Day?\nwords\nبَلَونَاهُمWe have tried them\nلَيَصرِمُنَّهَاTo harvest the fruits of their garden\nفَطَافَ عليهاIt was struck\nطَائِفٌAn affliction, a fire that destroyed it\nكَالصَّرِيمِAs black as night\nصَارِمِينَDetermined to harvest the crops\nعَلَى حَردٍDetermined to carry out their plan\nرَاغِبُونَTurn to our Lord in hope\nتَخَيَّرُونَWhatever you choose\nزَعِيمٌCan guarantee that"]])